<Layout title="Privacy Policy | Koursea Blog" description="Privacy policy for Koursea Blog, including analytics, advertising, cookies, third-party services and reader rights.">
  <article class="page prose"><p class="eyebrow">LAST UPDATED: SEPTEMBER 2, 2026</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="lead">This policy explains what information Koursea Blog may collect, why it is used, and the choices available to visitors.</p><h2>Information you provide</h2><p>If you contact us by email, we receive the information you choose to provide, such as your name, email address and message. We use it only to respond, investigate corrections, maintain records and protect the service.</p><h2>Automatically collected information</h2><p>Our hosting, security and analytics providers may process limited technical information such as IP address, browser type, device type, referring page, pages visited, approximate region and timestamps. We use this information to operate the website, diagnose problems, understand aggregate readership and prevent abuse.</p><h2>Cookies and local storage</h2><p>The site may use cookies or similar browser storage for essential preferences, analytics and advertising. Where legally required, non-essential storage will be activated only after appropriate notice or consent. You can clear or block cookies through your browser, although some features may then work differently.</p><h2>Advertising and Google AdSense</h2><p>We may use Google AdSense or another advertising provider. Google and its partners may use cookies or similar technologies to serve, measure and personalize advertising, subject to applicable consent requirements. Advertising providers may process device identifiers, interactions and approximate location. Learn more in Google’s <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener noreferrer">advertising policies</a> and use <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">My Ad Center</a> to manage Google advertising preferences.</p><h2>Third-party links</h2><p>Articles may link to maps, transit operators, tourism authorities, booking services and other websites. Their privacy practices are governed by their own policies. A link does not mean Koursea controls or endorses every statement on the linked service.</p><h2>How information is shared</h2><p>We do not sell personal information. Information may be shared with service providers that host, secure, measure or support the website; when required by law; or when necessary to protect users, the public or our legal rights. Providers are expected to process information only for defined operational purposes.</p><h2>Retention and security</h2><p>We retain contact messages and technical records only as long as reasonably needed for their purpose, legal obligations and security. No internet service can guarantee absolute security, but we use proportionate safeguards and limit access where practical.</p><h2>Children</h2><p>Koursea Blog is a general travel information service and is not directed to children under the age at which parental consent is required in their country. Please contact us if you believe a child has submitted personal information improperly.</p><h2>Your choices and rights</h2><p>Depending on your location, you may have rights to request access, correction, deletion, restriction or objection concerning personal information. You may also have the right to complain to a local data-protection authority. To make a request, email <a href="mailto:hello@koursea.com">hello@koursea.com</a>. We may need to verify the request.</p><h2>International processing</h2><p>Service providers may process data in countries other than your own. Where required, we rely on appropriate legal safeguards for international transfers.</p><h2>Policy updates</h2><p>We may update this policy when the site, providers or applicable requirements change. The latest version and update date will remain available on this page.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@koursea.com">hello@koursea.com</a>.</p></article>
